{
  "manufacturer": "Yaskawa",
  "manufacturer_slug": "yaskawa",
  "model": "P1000 Bypass for industrial fans and pumps (MEMOBUS/Modbus RTU)",
  "model_slug": "p1000-bypass",
  "short_model": "P1000 Bypass",
  "aliases": [
    "P1000 Bypass",
    "P1B"
  ],
  "equipment_type": "Variable frequency drive (HVAC bypass package)",
  "applies_to": "P1000 Bypass bypass controller RS-485 port with Z3-01 = 0 (Modbus); Technical Manual SIEP YAIP1B 01D, appendix D.",
  "summary": "The P1000 Bypass pairs the drive with a bypass controller board that has its own RS-485 port. Over Modbus RTU the bypass passes through the drive command and monitor registers and adds a bypass command word (run, AUTO select, BYPASS select, smoke purge, Motor AND/OR, fault reset), a bypass frequency reference, network control of the bypass inputs and outputs, and UB bypass monitors.",
  "transport": [
    "RTU"
  ],
  "defaults": {
    "unit_id": 1,
    "baud": 9600,
    "parity": "None",
    "data_bits": 8,
    "stop_bits": 1,
    "tcp_port": null
  },
  "addressing": {
    "convention": "hex 0-based",
    "note": "Register numbers are hex and are sent unchanged: the manual's read example asks for starting register 0020H as 00 20. Bypass parameters and monitors use the hex number printed under each one (Z3-01 = 8500H, UB-09 = 8788H)."
  },
  "default_word_order": null,
  "firmware": null,
  "source": {
    "title": "P1000 Bypass for industrial fans and pumps Technical Manual",
    "doc_number": "SIEP YAIP1B 01D",
    "revision_date": "2023-04",
    "url": "https://www.yaskawa.com/delegate/getAttachment?documentId=SIEPYAIP1B01&cmd=documents&documentName=SIEPYAIP1B01.pdf",
    "pages": "appendix D pp. 334-353 (Z3 parameters, message examples, D.9 MEMOBUS/Modbus data table), U: Monitors (UB) and parameter list"
  },
  "notes": [
    "All registers are 16-bit; signed values are noted per register.",
    "Frequency registers 8401H, 0023H and 0024H use the units chosen in drive parameter o1-03, so they are left unscaled.",
    "Bypass status and fault words UB-02 to UB-08 (8781H-8787H) are left out because the source shows their bits as display digits without a stated bit order.",
    "Left out: 0025H-0027H output voltage, current and power (unit switches or depends on model), 00ABH rated current, speed monitors in r/min, fault-trace blocks from 0080H and the fault/alarm description words from 00C0H.",
    "Function codes are 03H (read up to 16 registers), 08H (loopback) and 10H (write); there is no 06H.",
    "Z3-01 defaults to 3 (BACnet); select 0 for Modbus. Changes to the Z3 settings take effect after restarting.",
    "UB-17 contactor voltage is left out: the monitor table prints it at 878FH (the same number as UB-16) while the BACnet table puts it at 8790H.",
    "Z3-05 (comm fault action) is left out: its detail page gives range 0-3 but the parameter list adds setting 4 (run at Z3-10).",
    "8400H bits 9 and 11 are left out: the register table's row order gives HAND select and DRIVE select, but the BACnet object table in the same manual maps bit 9 to 'Drive Select' and bit 11 to 'Not Used'. The other 8400H bit numbers come from that BACnet table and agree with the row order."
  ],
